> to consistency for me.

I think part of this is because you're a serial ascender.  ;)

Once you pass a certain point in skill, the focus becomes significantly
different.  You no longer make the overall strategy mistakes that lead
to the "normal" deaths, so you focus more on the "unlucky"
instadeaths... saying to yourself, "well, I'll be fine unless I get
unlucky" and then start listing off the ways you can get unlucky.

So tins of PR might work out better for you.  But they're not a very
good overall recommendation, because far more people are far more likely
to make the basic strategy mistakes that lead to them getting their face
et.  For most people, it's better to not worry about corner-case
scenarios and focus on blocking the #1 killer; being hit to death.

